# Source Code Mode types as Typora's CodeMirror does. Enter goes on with
# a list or quote (numbers counting up, a task unticked), clears an empty
# item, leaves an empty quote, and keeps a line's indent; Shift+Enter is
# a bare new line. Brackets and quotes pair, typing the closer steps over
# it, Enter opens a line between braces, Backspace takes an empty pair
# back, and a quote typed over a selection wraps it. Tab indents the
# selected lines, Shift+Tab gives a line the indent above. The
# right-click menu has Cut, Copy and Paste only.
cmd sourceMode
check Ui.sourceMode && sourceView.edit.activeFocus && sourceView.edit.text === "\n"
type 1. one\ntwo\n\nafter\n- [x] done\nnext\n\n> quote\nmore\n\n    code\nx
check sourceView.edit.text === "1. one\n2. two\n\nafter\n- [x] done\n- [ ] next\n\n> quote\n> more\n> \n    code\n    x\n"
key Shift+Return
type f{\n(a) 'q' [
key BackSpace
type end
check sourceView.edit.text.endsWith("\n    x\nf{\n(a) 'q' end\n}\n")
eval sourceView.edit.select(sourceView.edit.text.indexOf("end"), sourceView.edit.text.indexOf("end") + 3)
type `
check sourceView.edit.text.endsWith("'q' `end`\n}\n") && sourceView.edit.selectedText === "end"
# The right-click menu has the clipboard only, and leaves the selection.
click 600 120 Right
wait 300
check sourceView.menu.visible && sourceView.menu.count === 3 && sourceView.menu.itemAt(2).text === "Paste"
check sourceView.edit.selectedText === "end"
key Escape
wait 100
check !sourceView.menu.visible
eval sourceView.edit.select(0, 2)
key Tab
check sourceView.edit.text.startsWith("    1. one\n2. two\n") && sourceView.edit.selectionStart === 0 && sourceView.edit.selectionEnd === 6
eval sourceView.edit.cursorPosition = sourceView.edit.text.indexOf("2. two") + 1
key Shift+Tab
check sourceView.edit.text.startsWith("    1. one\n    2. two\n") && sourceView.edit.cursorPosition === sourceView.edit.text.indexOf("2. two") + 1
cmd sourceMode
wait 300
dump @OUT@
